BEGIN_DESC
AtmoFX: a Delta Glider dives into the Great Red Spot (needs the AtmoFX fork of D3D9Client). The probe finds the Spot on the stock cloud map in the layer's current phase (MAPANCHOR u v) and puts the glider 1000 km up, 600 km west of its centre, flying east at 4 km/s relative to the air, 5 deg down. The Spot is ~16000 x 12000 km: from below ~3000 km you are inside it - an orange field of streaked clouds; as a spot it shows from 20000 km and more. Orbiter.log tells the sun elevation over the Spot: if it is night there, accelerate time (Jupiter turns in 3.75 h here) until the Spot is in daylight - the glider keeps falling, so restart the scenario after that if needed.
END_DESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 60970.5
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship JDG
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET JDG
  MODE Extern
  POS 3.00 -170.00 12.00
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 60.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Surface
END_HUD

BEGIN_SHIPS
Probe:AtmoProbe
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 0.00
  ALTKM 455
  MAPANCHOR 0.361 0.610
  CLOUDS 0
  LAUNCH JDG 1000 4 5 600
END
JDG:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 90.00
  RCSMODE 0
  AFCMODE 7
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000000 1:1.000000
  NAVFREQ 0 0 0 0
END
END_SHIPS
